# The kernel's source files, in link order, named once.
#
# Read by BOTH the cross build (Makefile) and the native one
# (build.sh, which runs on the machine itself). It exists because
# those two had separate copies of this list for about ten minutes
# and that was long enough to see how it would end: a file added to
# one, absent from the other, and a kernel that builds on the
# workstation and fails to link on the machine.
#
# Order matters. start.s is first because the vector table has to be
# at the start of the image -- the boot ROM reads its first two
# longwords as the initial SSP and PC.
#
# .s here is assembler-with-cpp, .c is C; the consumers split on the
# extension rather than being told twice.

start.s
memprobe.s
taskasm.s

